WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.449
The plan writes three
files: create dot sequel,

2
00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:08.825
cutover dot sequel and rollback dot
sequel, each with its S H A two fifty-six.

3
00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:11.262
A second person reads
them line by line and

4
00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:13.963
records the three hashes
in the change record.

5
00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:18.218
When the deploy runs, a file that doesn't
hash to its approved value is refused

6
00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:22.676
before anything connects, so the files
that run are the files that were approved.

7
00:00:22.676 --> 00:00:25.519
The deployer signs in as
its own Entra account,

8
00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:30.384
a member of the instance's Entra admin
group, activated under pim for the change

9
00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:35.100
window only, so that sys-admin, alter any
login and control server all read one.

10
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.073
And the book's Chapter 12, What the
Engine-Authentication Decision Settles,

11
00:00:39.073 --> 00:00:41.640
makes the parallel run
required for production.
